Please look out for Night, too.

151
06:34.690 --> 06:35.960
- Let's take some photos. - Night, Night, Night.

152
06:36.170 --> 06:37.850
Everyone’s in for some chills today!

153
06:37.880 --> 06:39.159
- Right. - They can become partners.

154
06:39.180 --> 06:40.550
The chemistry is through the roof.

155
06:42.730 --> 06:43.560
Ooh...

156
06:51.650 --> 06:53.159
Once a bottom, always a bottom.

157
06:56.500 --> 06:57.490
Lhao!

158
06:57.510 --> 06:59.440
She did it again. She made that face again!

159
06:59.890 --> 07:01.280
Take some photos while you wait.

160
07:01.990 --> 07:03.730
I'm getting you your name tag and script, okay?

161
07:04.630 --> 07:05.960
Mm...

162
07:05.980 --> 07:06.990
Go. You've got this.

163
07:07.010 --> 07:08.480
You've done so many things now. Go.

164
07:19.240 --> 07:20.130
[Register]

165
07:20.150 --> 07:21.880
Yes, Wan's.

166
07:22.620 --> 07:24.280
Thank you. That's everything?

167
07:25.540 --> 07:26.300
Alright.

168
07:26.380 --> 07:27.400
Thank you.

169
07:32.120 --> 07:32.840
Cher.

170
07:35.190 --> 07:35.720
Here you go,

171
07:36.330 --> 07:36.900
your name tag.

172
07:36.920 --> 07:37.600
[Wan]

173
07:38.400 --> 07:39.710
Here's your script.

174
07:46.100 --> 07:46.890
Cher,

175
07:47.510 --> 07:48.730
don't you think it's odd?

176
07:49.400 --> 07:51.400
The script is just like the audition for 'The Deep Between Us.'

177
07:52.360 --> 07:53.659
Well... No.

178
07:54.040 --> 07:54.840
Completely normal.

179
08:01.170 --> 08:01.800
[Jay]

180
08:03.820 --> 08:04.640
What? Hey!

181
08:04.840 --> 08:06.330
- Jay. - Oh!

182
08:06.540 --> 08:07.540
Hey, man.

183
08:07.640 --> 08:08.880
You're here to audition?

184
08:09.050 --> 08:10.220
Hell yeah, man.

185
08:10.240 --> 08:11.450
I want to be an actor.

186
08:11.980 --> 08:13.720
This one character's a good fit for me.

187
08:13.800 --> 08:15.680
He's Jess, the bottom male lead's friend.

188
08:16.750 --> 08:18.430
Mm...

189
08:18.620 --> 08:19.960
How about this, man?

190
08:21.000 --> 08:22.370
If you make the cut,

191
08:23.010 --> 08:24.210
how about you eat some dog food?

192
08:24.660 --> 08:26.200
Got the balls?

193
08:26.220 --> 08:27.340
I'm game!

194
08:27.360 --> 08:28.170
If I really make the cut,

195
08:28.190 --> 08:29.480
I'm eating the whole damn can.

196
08:29.930 --> 08:30.860
Good.

197
08:31.100 --> 08:33.030
Pick a flavor, then. Which one do you want?

198
08:33.049 --> 08:36.120
Liver or chicken in gravy?

199
08:38.000 --> 08:40.080
Was the one you ate yummy?

200
08:40.740 --> 08:42.510
You bet your ass it was!

201
08:42.539 --> 08:43.750
Then I'll go with that one, punk.

202
08:45.590 --> 08:46.600
Jay, are you signed with any company?

203
08:48.840 --> 08:49.510
How about Our House?

204
08:49.530 --> 08:50.740
I'll have to think about it.

205
08:50.760 --> 08:51.880
It seems quite chaotic.

206
08:53.200 --> 08:53.920
Hey...

207
08:54.230 --> 08:55.160
It's not.

208
08:55.180 --> 08:56.080
Look at me.

209
08:56.990 --> 08:58.160
Yeah, I did look at you,

210
08:58.180 --> 08:59.280
the most chaotic of all.

211
08:59.750 --> 09:01.620
♫I'm ready to leave it all behind♫

212
09:01.640 --> 09:03.500
♫Just so I could claim the sky♫

213
09:03.520 --> 09:05.400
♫I'd sacrifice my being♫

214
09:05.420 --> 09:08.870
♫Without looking back and regretting♫

215
09:08.890 --> 09:11.960
♫For the end I yearn for in my veins♫

216
09:13.760 --> 09:14.680
Thank you.

217
09:14.700 --> 09:15.680
Alright.

218
09:16.960 --> 09:18.240
Jay,

219
09:18.260 --> 09:19.440
your character matches...

220
09:19.740 --> 09:21.460
the role of Win's friend.

221
09:21.480 --> 09:22.080
Yes,

222
09:22.170 --> 09:23.040
a pretty good match.

223
09:23.720 --> 09:24.440
A perfect match.

224
09:24.790 --> 09:25.680
Though...

225
09:25.890 --> 09:27.960
hang tight until the audition result comes out.

226
09:28.310 --> 09:28.950
Alright.

227
09:28.970 --> 09:30.050
- Thank you for today. - Thank you.

228
09:30.070 --> 09:30.500
Right.

229
09:30.520 --> 09:31.860
- Thank you. - Good luck.

230
09:31.880 --> 09:32.640
Alright.

231
09:32.860 --> 09:34.160
Let's rock and roll, chat.

232
09:35.440 --> 09:36.160
How does that sound?

233
09:37.310 --> 09:39.450
You talk like a Gen Zer but you sound like a millennial.

234
09:39.700 --> 09:41.940
Well, I'm a Gen Zer. Who said I'm...

235
09:41.960 --> 09:42.860
Ooh, here he comes.

236
09:47.760 --> 09:48.560
Whoa!

237
09:57.260 --> 09:58.240
You knew about this?

238
10:01.820 --> 10:02.480
Right,

239
10:02.890 --> 10:05.120
you're auditioning for Win, right?

240
10:05.640 --> 10:06.300
Yes.

241
10:06.650 --> 10:09.720
So if you're ready,

242
10:10.020 --> 10:12.240
concentrate and get started.

243
10:31.080 --> 10:32.240
"Huh... Is this

244
10:32.260 --> 10:34.700
the promising young shark Coach praises so much?

245
10:35.060 --> 10:36.930
All I can see is a fucking loser."

246
10:36.950 --> 10:37.770
Terrible.

247
10:37.790 --> 10:38.570
Whoa...

248
10:45.640 --> 10:48.940
[Third]

249
10:48.960 --> 10:52.260
[Wan]

250
11:05.890 --> 11:07.250
Oh, my God...

251
11:46.640 --> 11:48.550
Want me to show you what superior acting looks like?

252
12:00.250 --> 12:01.250
Only look at me.

253
12:02.770 --> 12:03.740
Only listen to me.

254
12:15.850 --> 12:16.850
Stay with me.

255
12:34.060 --> 12:35.540
Show me how it's done.

256
12:37.260 --> 12:40.050
From what I've seen in the series, you're not all that.

257
12:42.270 --> 12:43.420
Run the scene with me, then.

258
12:45.380 --> 12:47.000
But you'll have to improvise.

259
12:49.260 --> 12:50.540
If you're ready, you can go first.

260
12:51.790 --> 12:52.850
I'm giving you a head start.

261
12:59.710 --> 13:00.480
Cut!

262
13:02.860 --> 13:03.720
That was good,

263
13:03.880 --> 13:04.550
alright?

264
13:04.860 --> 13:05.660
Let's leave it there.

265
13:05.680 --> 13:06.760
- Yeah? - True. He's right.

266
13:07.100 --> 13:10.160
Staff, please remove all the water from the set.

267
13:10.240 --> 13:10.890
Take it away.

268
13:10.910 --> 13:12.030
Or history would repeat itself.

269
13:12.050 --> 13:13.540
I don't wanna get soaked, you see.

270
13:14.520 --> 13:16.010
Since the roles already called for the actors...

271
13:16.310 --> 13:16.960
Wait...

272
13:17.380 --> 13:19.080
Or is it that the actors called for the roles?

273
13:33.880 --> 13:34.530
Wan!

274
13:35.960 --> 13:36.920
How was it?

275
13:38.690 --> 13:39.250
Mm...

276
13:39.270 --> 13:40.780
Everyone is just the same, Cher.

277
13:40.800 --> 13:42.360
Except for Luang.

278
13:42.480 --> 13:45.080
[LUANG IN YOUR AREA]

279
13:46.330 --> 13:47.980
Well, his boss is a Gen Zer.

280
13:48.070 --> 13:49.440
He's gotta make some changes, right?

281
13:56.780 --> 13:57.780
I...

282
13:59.640 --> 14:00.370
Wan,

283
14:01.880 --> 14:02.880
I want to talk to you for a moment.

284
14:10.240 --> 14:11.860
Go talk it over.

285
14:12.330 --> 14:13.190
Let bygones

286
14:13.210 --> 14:14.670
be bygones.

287
14:14.690 --> 14:16.780
It's better to begin again and do it the right way.

288
14:16.800 --> 14:18.170
Live in the present, yeah?

289
14:22.690 --> 14:24.840
Thank you for bringing Wan back to me, Cher.

290
14:27.140 --> 14:28.250
Are you gonna take long, Third?

291
14:28.480 --> 14:29.840
I've gotta rush to take care of some work.

292
14:30.400 --> 14:31.680
Feel free to head out.

293
14:32.340 --> 14:33.370
I'll give him a ride.

294
14:34.490 --> 14:36.300
Let Third drop you off. I'll get going now.

295
14:37.780 --> 14:38.680
Cher...

296
14:40.070 --> 14:41.060
It's fine.

297
14:41.080 --> 14:42.560
You never had a problem with it back then.

298
14:42.880 --> 14:44.080
I'm allowing it this time.

299
14:45.200 --> 14:45.880
Go.

300
14:46.390 --> 14:47.750
Acting like it's so impossible

301
14:47.770 --> 14:49.050
after you pulled a fast one on me back then.

302
14:49.070 --> 14:50.070
I was almost in deep shit!

303
15:25.560 --> 15:27.150
I'm glad you came today.

304
15:32.820 --> 15:34.790
I'm glad to see you, too.

305
15:38.300 --> 15:39.360
You know?

306
15:39.950 --> 15:40.500
Last night...

307
15:40.520 --> 15:41.910
before the audition,

308
15:43.020 --> 15:45.080
I thought about the first day we met.

309
15:47.320 --> 15:48.500
Send in the guards, please.

310
15:49.320 --> 15:51.000
There's a stalking sasaeng in here.

311
15:51.320 --> 15:52.370
A hidden gem!

312
15:53.520 --> 15:56.340
I thought about the day I stumbled into that audition

313
15:56.360 --> 15:57.580
because I met Cher.

314
15:58.910 --> 16:01.000
That was how I met you again.

315
16:01.100 --> 16:02.170
"Huh... Is this

316
16:02.190 --> 16:04.010
the promising young shark Coach praises so much?"

317
16:04.030 --> 16:05.040
Terrible.

318
16:05.950 --> 16:07.120
Show me how it's done,

319
16:07.140 --> 16:08.080
since you're so good.

320
16:08.370 --> 16:10.720
From what I've seen in the series, you're not all that.

321
16:12.160 --> 16:13.360
Watch your behavior, though,

322
16:13.610 --> 16:16.000
or people will call you a "stalking sasaeng."

323
16:16.350 --> 16:17.760
Even though you insulted me so much

324
16:18.260 --> 16:19.810
that my blood boiled,

325
16:20.110 --> 16:21.320
and that I felt so suffocated

326
16:21.900 --> 16:23.610
that you had to come to my rescue,

327
16:24.910 --> 16:27.030
that improv technique of yours

328
16:27.370 --> 16:28.670
was how I made the cut.

329
16:28.690 --> 16:30.560
Shit, you made the cut?!

330
16:31.040 --> 16:32.800
[Ashawin Kosonkasem] [Artist]

331
16:33.350 --> 16:34.470
Because of you...

332
16:35.170 --> 16:36.920
I paid off my parents' debt.

333
16:37.400 --> 16:38.900
As long as I pay it off for Mom,

334
16:38.920 --> 16:40.040
I'm happy.

335
16:41.130 --> 16:42.160
Because of you...

336
16:43.120 --> 16:45.120
I got into the entertainment industry.

337
16:48.450 --> 16:49.160
Cut!

338
16:49.820 --> 16:51.820
Wan, it's been so many takes,

339
16:51.840 --> 16:53.280
and none of them worked!

340
16:53.560 --> 16:56.540
Even though my ABCs of acting started from nothing...

341
16:56.560 --> 16:57.800
You haven't got a clue!

342
16:58.190 --> 17:00.400
Do you suppose we're ever gonna understand Sky?

343
17:00.720 --> 17:01.800
But because of you,

344
17:02.320 --> 17:04.220
you taught me to understand the emotions

345
17:04.560 --> 17:06.210
and feelings of the character.

346
17:07.819 --> 17:08.800
Only look at me.

347
17:10.319 --> 17:11.310
Only listen to me.

348
17:12.400 --> 17:13.400
Stay with me.

349
17:15.900 --> 17:16.980
You did amazingly today.

350
17:18.079 --> 17:19.800
Are you seriously complimenting me?

351
17:20.680 --> 17:22.119
And most importantly,

352
17:22.900 --> 17:25.319
you taught me to understand my own feelings

353
17:26.660 --> 17:28.560
and how it feels to be loved.

354
17:36.870 --> 17:39.520
I don't know exactly when we fell for each other,

355
17:40.080 --> 17:41.760
but before I realized it,

356
17:43.090 --> 17:44.720
you were already a part of my life.

357
17:45.200 --> 17:45.880
Wan.

358
17:46.570 --> 17:47.880
Do you trust your man, Wan?

359
17:48.760 --> 17:50.920
Of course, your boy trusts you.

360
17:51.350 --> 17:52.360
What are you drawing?

361
17:52.530 --> 17:53.440
An elephant.

362
17:53.780 --> 17:55.440
But you're even cuter.

363
17:56.390 --> 17:57.400
You like being with me, huh?

364
17:58.700 --> 17:59.880
I think so.

365
18:02.510 --> 18:03.510
Despite the grueling situations

366
18:03.540 --> 18:05.920
along the way,

367
18:06.930 --> 18:08.440
we came through.

368
18:17.150 --> 18:18.760
I give up.

369
18:19.370 --> 18:20.600
Wut...

370
18:21.250 --> 18:24.160
Still, so many people were left with scars.

371
18:26.000 --> 18:27.470
Falling from where I am might hurt,

372
18:28.590 --> 18:29.920
but I won't be embarrassed.

373
18:30.030 --> 18:31.280
Please don't go, Nine.

374
18:31.690 --> 18:32.320
Nine!

375
18:32.450 --> 18:32.950
Nine, baby!!

376
18:32.970 --> 18:33.580
Wan!

377
18:33.600 --> 18:34.170
Grab him.

378
18:34.190 --> 18:35.240
I'm sorry.

379
18:35.620 --> 18:38.280
I should've cared more about you guys.

380
18:39.200 --> 18:41.180
Including you and me

381
18:41.920 --> 18:43.800
who also needed time to heal.

382
18:44.720 --> 18:45.830
Let's break up.

383
18:46.830 --> 18:48.100
Don't leave, please?

384
18:48.120 --> 18:49.340
Stay with me.

385
18:49.360 --> 18:52.760
I hope you get to chase your dream with all you've got.

386
18:54.670 --> 18:56.600
No, Wan.

387
18:56.890 --> 18:57.660
Wan...

388
18:58.260 --> 18:58.960
Wan...

389
19:00.430 --> 19:02.280
After all this time,

390
19:02.410 --> 19:04.920
I have reflected on every single one of my thoughts.

391
19:05.920 --> 19:08.760
It made me understand my own feelings.

392
19:09.940 --> 19:12.000
No matter how long the world keeps spinning,

393
19:13.200 --> 19:15.960
my feelings for you...

394
19:18.020 --> 19:19.640
stay the same.

395
19:38.710 --> 19:40.720
Can we start over?

396
19:51.170 --> 19:52.380
But I'm a sasaeng.

397
19:58.580 --> 20:00.180
I won't call the guards on you this time.

398
20:28.370 --> 20:30.170
And I will hold you tight.

399
20:33.480 --> 20:35.200
I won't ever let you run from me again.

400
20:43.420 --> 20:44.600
I'm sorry

401
20:46.860 --> 20:48.330
for everything.

402
21:19.610 --> 21:21.320
I'm sorry, too,

403
21:22.800 --> 21:24.320
that I only thought about myself.

404
21:25.760 --> 21:26.590
I...

405
21:26.610 --> 21:27.750
didn't even love myself.

406
21:30.070 --> 21:32.480
I put you through so much and then walked away from you.

407
21:40.480 --> 21:41.400
Wan.

408
21:46.440 --> 21:47.820
I love you, Wan.

409
21:54.170 --> 21:55.920
I want to see you.

410
21:58.460 --> 21:59.670
I want to be with you.

411
22:03.760 --> 22:05.180
I want to be possessive of you.

412
22:05.200 --> 22:06.380
I want to get jealous over you.

413
22:08.770 --> 22:10.120
I want to worry about you.

414
22:20.120 --> 22:21.600
Let me win your heart again, please?

415
22:23.060 --> 22:23.880
Please?

416
23:00.480 --> 23:01.520
Winning my heart

417
23:03.690 --> 23:04.750
isn't easy.

418
23:14.370 --> 23:15.080
Sure.

419
23:18.270 --> 23:19.770
I'll keep on...

420
23:21.010 --> 23:22.040
flirting.

421
23:22.990 --> 23:25.000
Don't try to avoid me

422
23:25.020 --> 23:27.960
'cause I won't stop

423
23:28.460 --> 23:30.720
till you fall for me.

424
23:31.620 --> 23:34.360
I'll keep on flirting.

425
23:34.960 --> 23:36.800
I won't stop, I guarantee.

426
23:37.260 --> 23:40.480
I'll love you hard.

427
23:46.870 --> 23:51.280
♫And once you say yes, I'll set you free♫

428
23:59.390 --> 24:00.390
So delusional.

429
24:03.170 --> 24:04.170
Do you like it, though?

430
24:07.900 --> 24:09.520
I freaking love it.

431
24:57.110 --> 24:57.990
What would happen

432
24:58.010 --> 25:00.120
if I woke up and found out that this was all a dream?

433
25:01.160 --> 25:02.440
It's time to wake up, then.

434
25:02.590 --> 25:03.440
Huh?!

435
25:04.420 --> 25:05.600
Am I dreaming?

436
25:06.200 --> 25:07.340
No, no, no, no,

437
25:07.360 --> 25:08.920
I'm not waking up.

438
25:09.420 --> 25:10.700
I'm gonna ask to hold you first.

439
25:10.820 --> 25:12.120
Let me hold you first...

440
25:15.760 --> 25:17.960
I think I should head home. It's getting late.

441
25:18.590 --> 25:19.850
Hey, wait!

442
25:19.870 --> 25:21.030
Are you leaving already?

443
25:21.130 --> 25:22.150
Can you stay?

444
25:22.170 --> 25:23.410
I still want to spend time with you...

445
25:23.430 --> 25:24.470
No!

446
25:24.490 --> 25:25.560
Please?

447
25:28.650 --> 25:29.440
Please?

448
25:31.550 --> 25:33.800
Please, please?

449
25:53.690 --> 25:55.740
More, more, more.

450
25:55.760 --> 25:57.160
That's already too much.

451
25:57.450 --> 25:58.470
Please?

452
26:02.480 --> 26:03.750
Let go!

453
26:03.860 --> 26:04.860
Just for a minute.

454
26:04.880 --> 26:06.760
I'll give you a ride to your condo.

455
26:09.050 --> 26:10.060
I'll give you ten.

456
26:10.550 --> 26:11.340
Okay,

457
26:11.360 --> 26:12.090
ten minutes.

458
26:12.110 --> 26:12.760
Ten...

459
26:13.360 --> 26:14.480
- Nine... - Whoa!

460
26:14.730 --> 26:15.240
Eight...

461
26:15.600 --> 26:16.280
Seven...

462
26:17.310 --> 26:17.920
Six...

463
26:18.580 --> 26:19.910
Five, four, three, two, one, zero.

464
26:19.930 --> 26:21.200
Wait, hey!

465
26:21.220 --> 26:22.040
Time's up!

466
26:22.880 --> 26:23.380
Halt!

467
26:23.410 --> 26:23.900
Halt!

468
26:23.920 --> 26:24.860
Halt!!

469
26:33.880 --> 26:35.360
Pretty please?

470
26:38.520 --> 26:40.440
Just retake that Animal Exercise class.

471
26:40.660 --> 26:42.160
Luang's gotta be bawling 'cause of this.

472
26:44.150 --> 26:44.960
Okay,

473
26:47.280 --> 26:48.600
I'm getting into the lesson, then.

474
27:05.080 --> 27:06.260
Don't!

475
27:06.280 --> 27:07.520
I'm not letting you go...

476
27:08.190 --> 27:09.880
No...

477
27:11.650 --> 27:12.440
Come on.

478
27:12.560 --> 27:13.410
Are you giving me a ride or what?

479
27:13.430 --> 27:14.200
Let's go. Get up.

480
27:20.670 --> 27:21.960
Shoot me with the update.

481
27:23.670 --> 27:27.050
So, right now, the team and I have agreed that

482
27:27.070 --> 27:29.570
when it comes to the main cast of 'Mr. Fanboy Series,'

483
27:29.590 --> 27:31.830
the two male leads have to be Third and Wan.

484
27:33.350 --> 27:33.830
Alright.

485
27:33.860 --> 27:35.020
We're on the same page.

486
27:35.040 --> 27:36.700
I finished the novel you wrote, Time,

487
27:36.720 --> 27:37.760
'Mr. Fanboy,' I mean.

488
27:38.150 --> 27:39.760
As for the screenwriting team,

489
27:39.780 --> 27:41.120
they're outlining the dialogue.

490
27:42.430 --> 27:43.680
Any thoughts? Do you like it?

491
27:43.700 --> 27:44.720
It was such a fun read.

492
27:44.740 --> 27:47.320
Wow, the story's timing and narrative dynamics are awesome.

493
27:47.340 --> 27:49.170
More than that, it's realistic.

494
27:49.190 --> 27:50.960
Feels like it has actual life to it or something.

495
27:51.310 --> 27:51.790
Oh...

496
27:51.810 --> 27:53.800
Not just "feels like."

497
27:53.820 --> 27:54.830
It has actual "lives" to it, alright.

498
27:54.850 --> 27:56.400
And I can tell who they are.

499
27:57.290 --> 27:58.660
I tried to twist it.

500
27:58.680 --> 28:00.310
Like, I tried to change the details.

501
28:00.330 --> 28:00.990
Still...

502
28:01.630 --> 28:03.280
it’s too close to reality, right?

503
28:03.300 --> 28:04.480
- Good call on twisting it. - You... You did.

504
28:04.500 --> 28:05.120
- You did? - If...

505
28:05.140 --> 28:07.110
If you didn't twist it, it would've turned into a documentary.

506
28:07.130 --> 28:08.440
It would've been too realistic, you see.

507
28:15.010 --> 28:17.040
Jay, you're gonna get it...

508
28:17.460 --> 28:18.310
You have to make the cut.

509
28:18.330 --> 28:20.860
If not, where would these even go?

510
28:21.990 --> 28:24.240
Wan, my guy.

511
28:24.260 --> 28:25.360
Uh... What's up, my guy?

512
28:27.160 --> 28:27.870
What are you up to?

513
28:27.890 --> 28:29.240
Uh, nothing.

514
28:30.860 --> 28:32.120
So did you make the cut?

515
28:32.460 --> 28:33.340
I don't know.

516
28:33.600 --> 28:34.770
Cher hasn't said anything.

517
28:34.790 --> 28:36.000
What about you? Did you?

518
28:39.860 --> 28:42.080
I'll take the chicken in gravy.

519
28:43.340 --> 28:44.760
Don't you worry.

520
28:45.060 --> 28:46.300
I have it prepared.

521
28:46.390 --> 28:46.940
So that's mine.

522
28:46.960 --> 28:47.910
Bam!

523
28:47.930 --> 28:49.040
Dog food.

524
28:49.860 --> 28:51.070
Wait, there's more.

525
28:51.100 --> 28:52.120
Bam!

526
28:52.140 --> 28:53.170
These are on the house.

527
28:53.200 --> 28:54.880
Shampoo for when you wanna shower.

528
28:54.900 --> 28:55.760
There's more.

529
28:56.300 --> 28:57.440
Perfume spray

530
28:57.560 --> 28:59.560
so you smell nice and rich.

531
28:59.720 --> 29:00.630
Take them, take them.

532
29:00.650 --> 29:02.760
I'm becoming an actor, not a dog!

533
29:02.910 --> 29:05.000
Please, I'm the bottom male lead's friend!

534
29:05.050 --> 29:05.740
I know!

535
29:06.070 --> 29:07.560
And here they are, my good intentions.

536
29:07.580 --> 29:08.490
Now, his friend's gonna smell nice

537
29:08.510 --> 29:09.680
- and divine. Take it. - No way!

538
29:09.700 --> 29:11.880
- Here you go. - This is all I've promised, so this is it!

539
29:14.620 --> 29:15.460
What's going on?

540
29:15.480 --> 29:17.290
- It's Jay! - No. Nothing at all.

541
29:17.310 --> 29:18.290
Just had a meal,

542
29:18.310 --> 29:19.760
and I'm all bloated. Look.

543
29:21.380 --> 29:22.050
Wan,

544
29:22.070 --> 29:23.730
the series' account hinted they already cast the roles.

545
29:23.750 --> 29:24.580
Did you get the role?

546
29:25.400 --> 29:26.010
[From a novel based on the true story of a set's behind-the-scenes

547
29:26.030 --> 29:26.720
to 'Mr. Fanboy Series,'

548
29:26.740 --> 29:27.350
coming soon]

549
29:27.370 --> 29:28.470
Did you make the cut?

550
29:29.370 --> 29:30.370
I don't know.

551
29:30.750 --> 29:31.750
But...

552
29:32.150 --> 29:33.340
Jay made the cut!

553
29:33.360 --> 29:35.260
Whoa, really?!

554
29:35.640 --> 29:36.820
Jeez...

555
29:36.840 --> 29:39.580
Wanna go ahead and ask for my autograph, sis?

556
29:41.450 --> 29:42.560
I wanna know about yours.

557
29:43.010 --> 29:44.050
Call Cher.

558
29:45.500 --> 29:46.310
Quick.

559
29:51.560 --> 29:52.640
Hello, girlie.

560
29:52.660 --> 29:54.660
What's up, girlie?

561
29:55.450 --> 29:55.910
So...

562
29:55.940 --> 29:57.570
the voices in my head took the W.

563
29:57.590 --> 29:58.720
Did Wan make the cut?

564
30:01.000 --> 30:04.000
Wait, what do those laughs mean, girlie?

565
30:06.670 --> 30:08.070
Tell Wan

566
30:08.190 --> 30:10.160
that we're meeting the producers tomorrow

567
30:10.240 --> 30:12.680
- because he made the cut! - Whoa!

568
30:15.270 --> 30:16.760
See you tomorrow at 8 A.M.

569
30:16.780 --> 30:17.930
I'll pick you up at your condo, Wan.

570
30:17.950 --> 30:18.450
Alright,

571
30:18.470 --> 30:19.720
sure thing, Cher.

572
30:23.450 --> 30:24.880
That's what I'm talking about!

573
30:26.060 --> 30:26.970
Isn't that right?

574
30:26.990 --> 30:30.920
Cause this is the place where every dream comes true!

575
30:31.820 --> 30:34.130
- Yay! - Yay!

576
30:34.280 --> 30:35.240
Attaboy.

577
30:35.950 --> 30:38.240
I pray that no trouble comes your way this time.

578
30:38.260 --> 30:39.830
May you find yourself a nice crowd

579
30:39.850 --> 30:42.200
and become a global star, brother!

580
30:42.850 --> 30:44.950
- Sadhu! - Sadhu!

581
30:46.060 --> 30:47.180
Hey, what about you, Jay?

582
30:47.200 --> 30:47.870
Huh?

583
30:48.740 --> 30:50.260
- What? - You!

584
30:50.750 --> 30:51.960
He's gonna eat dog food!

585
30:51.980 --> 30:52.780
I'm not...

586
30:52.800 --> 30:53.400
You're right!

587
30:53.420 --> 30:55.730
- I'm just bloated after a meal. - See? Look at that.

588
30:55.750 --> 30:57.330
I have to take a shit.

589
30:57.640 --> 30:59.000
Can I take a shit first?

590
31:03.290 --> 31:04.880
Congratulations, Wan.

591
31:05.420 --> 31:07.740
In the end, you did it.

592
31:07.760 --> 31:09.520
You finally made it through.

593
31:09.580 --> 31:10.840
Amazing job!

594
31:12.950 --> 31:16.510
Well, thank you for giving me a chance.

595
31:17.750 --> 31:19.000
You too, Cher.

596
31:23.490 --> 31:24.360
Though, I do think

597
31:24.380 --> 31:26.480
I have it in me to become the company's legend?

598
31:26.640 --> 31:27.860
You are a legend, alright.

599
31:28.260 --> 31:29.080
Wut and I

600
31:29.100 --> 31:30.960
were balding so bad we almost lost all our hair.

601
31:31.610 --> 31:32.720
I have gray hair, too.

602
31:33.170 --> 31:35.280
I used up a whole carton of box dyes to cover it up.

603
31:36.840 --> 31:38.430
Um...

604
31:39.020 --> 31:41.600
So, if I want to work here again,

605
31:41.730 --> 31:44.040
I'm not sure about the documents...

606
31:45.060 --> 31:47.840
You mean the Termination of Artist Contract?

607
31:48.450 --> 31:49.260
Ugh!

608
31:49.280 --> 31:52.640
I fed that paper to the goats ages ago

609
31:55.060 --> 31:56.690
cause I always knew...

610
31:56.710 --> 31:59.700
you'd come back no matter what.

611
32:00.250 --> 32:02.160
Well, I'm sure that...

612
32:02.420 --> 32:03.230
this house

613
32:03.250 --> 32:05.110
will make every dream

614
32:05.130 --> 32:07.240
come true!

615
32:10.440 --> 32:11.180
Oh, goodness!

616
32:11.910 --> 32:12.570
The tears...

617
32:12.590 --> 32:14.020
Ugh, goodness. Give me a hug!

618
32:14.040 --> 32:15.550
Alright, bring it in.

619
32:15.790 --> 32:17.840
I'm so proud of my baby!

620
32:18.950 --> 32:20.450
Cher, quick. Join our group hug.

621
32:24.430 --> 32:27.230
Our butts are saved. No more shutting this place down!

622
32:27.250 --> 32:29.360
Uh... if that’s the case,

623
32:30.030 --> 32:31.820
don't forget to pay me back 10,000 baht.

624
32:33.200 --> 32:33.800
What was that for?

625
32:33.940 --> 32:34.660
Well...

626
32:34.790 --> 32:36.720
For taking Wan to the audition.

627
32:38.030 --> 32:40.280
Ah, I remember it now.

628
32:40.300 --> 32:41.000
Uh, wait.

629
32:41.140 --> 32:42.240
It's actually 15,000.

630
32:42.260 --> 32:43.480
15,000 baht.

631
32:43.650 --> 32:44.800
Where's the other 5,000 from?

632
32:44.950 --> 32:46.780
The first audition for 'The Deep Between Us.'

633
32:48.440 --> 32:49.350
Smart!

634
32:49.630 --> 32:51.930
Excellent memory, indeed.

635
32:51.950 --> 32:55.250
So how come you always fumble the schedules so terribly?

636
32:56.010 --> 32:57.430
Well, the schedules are packed

637
32:57.450 --> 32:58.720
but I don't get paid enough.

638
32:59.750 --> 33:00.860
Fine, I'll wire it to you.

639
33:02.140 --> 33:04.220
And hurry up and take Wan upstairs.

640
33:04.240 --> 33:06.420
I've told the team to prepare everything.

641
33:06.440 --> 33:08.100
You know what you have to do, right?

642
33:08.750 --> 33:11.560
It's the Star Glamour time!

643
33:12.170 --> 33:13.030
Oops, I'm mistaken.

644
33:13.050 --> 33:14.600
For you, it has to be

645
33:14.710 --> 33:18.720
the Star Glamour time, "once again"!

646
33:21.290 --> 33:23.140
Reborn. Rebirth.

647
33:23.160 --> 33:23.850
Right on.

648
33:23.870 --> 33:24.640
You're free today, right?

649
33:24.660 --> 33:25.980
There's so much to be done,

650
33:26.000 --> 33:27.540
but first things first...

651
33:27.580 --> 33:28.520
Taking headshots.

652
33:29.270 --> 33:30.040
Excellent.

653
33:30.240 --> 33:31.040
- Let's go. - Let's go.

654
33:31.060 --> 33:32.430
Fabulous. Make sure you rock it.

655
33:32.450 --> 33:32.960
Alright.

656
33:32.980 --> 33:33.650
Oh?

657
33:37.060 --> 33:38.060
Hello, Cher.

658
33:38.080 --> 33:39.120
Hello, Wut.

659
33:39.350 --> 33:40.550
Hello, Wan.

660
33:40.570 --> 33:41.530
Hello.

661
33:41.550 --> 33:42.500
This is Pung,

662
33:42.520 --> 33:44.720
the brand-new kid on the block.

663
33:45.530 --> 33:46.480
Uh, Wan,

664
33:46.540 --> 33:48.900
I've always been a fan of your work.

665
33:49.140 --> 33:50.600
I'm so glad you're back.

666
33:51.920 --> 33:53.430
Right, you're now the senior.

667
33:53.450 --> 33:55.000
Hype him up a little.

668
33:58.690 --> 33:59.520
Is that a good idea?

669
33:59.960 --> 34:02.840
Come on, it's like how that senior hyped you up.

670
34:03.100 --> 34:04.440
Go on.

671
34:15.880 --> 34:16.929
Good luck, boy.

672
34:17.469 --> 34:19.260
One day, you'll be as famous as me.

673
34:19.290 --> 34:22.610
So famous that you wanna flee from the industry!

674
34:25.400 --> 34:27.010
A big-name superstar.

675
34:29.889 --> 34:32.000
Wow! Global kind of vibe.

676
34:34.270 --> 34:35.320
Let's go, Cher.

677
34:35.989 --> 34:37.280
Perfect.

678
34:37.530 --> 34:38.719
You really copy-pasted the guy.

679
34:38.739 --> 34:40.320
Keep a close eye on him, Cher.

680
34:40.670 --> 34:41.730
Alright, Kendall.

681
34:41.750 --> 34:42.840
Go trim your bangs.

682
34:42.889 --> 34:43.900
They're not even.

683
34:44.360 --> 34:45.219
Please.

684
34:45.239 --> 34:46.120
Thank you.

685
34:51.239 --> 34:52.340
Your name is Pung, right?

686
34:52.360 --> 34:53.230
That's right.

687
34:53.250 --> 34:54.639
Welcome.

688
34:54.940 --> 34:56.500
You've made the right decision

689
34:56.520 --> 34:57.960
signing with us

690
34:58.530 --> 35:00.080
because this place

691
35:00.160 --> 35:02.360
makes every dream

692
35:02.710 --> 35:05.920
come true!

693
35:09.260 --> 35:10.020
Isn't it cute?

694
35:10.040 --> 35:11.690
- It is. - Come on. Give it a try.

695
35:11.710 --> 35:13.750
"This place makes every dream

696
35:13.770 --> 35:15.460
come true!"

697
35:15.480 --> 35:17.370
Add more flow to it.

698
35:17.390 --> 35:18.600
Go with the tide.

699
35:18.690 --> 35:20.430
"This place makes every dream

700
35:20.450 --> 35:22.300
come true!"

701
35:22.320 --> 35:24.000
Wow, superb hand movement.

702
35:24.050 --> 35:26.250
- Trust me. You're starting off with a bang. - Right.

703
35:26.270 --> 35:28.880
- Thank you. - Okay!

704
35:31.860 --> 35:33.240
Let's get down to business.

705
35:33.580 --> 35:35.210
I invited you all here today

706
35:35.230 --> 35:38.120
to prepare to announce the shooting of 'Mr. Fanboy Series.'

707
35:38.380 --> 35:40.100
Our leading men are

708
35:40.120 --> 35:41.120
Third and Wan.

709
35:41.940 --> 35:43.240
At this year's lineup event,

710
35:43.260 --> 35:44.830
we'll introduce both of you.

711
35:45.020 --> 35:46.930
Casting a real-life couple like this...

712
35:47.690 --> 35:48.800
it's gonna go viral.

713
35:50.230 --> 35:52.150
I'm sorry, Third, Wan,

714
35:52.170 --> 35:55.000
for adapting your story into a novel without asking.

715
35:56.040 --> 35:56.920
You're fine.

716
35:57.130 --> 35:58.480
But I agree with this

717
35:58.670 --> 36:01.680
because ThirdWan's chemistry is through the roof.

718
36:02.430 --> 36:03.120
Look,

719
36:04.240 --> 36:06.080
just their eye contact alone...

720
36:23.370 --> 36:24.900
Then, I'm gonna go ahead and confess.

721
36:25.720 --> 36:27.240
When they were on camera,

722
36:27.490 --> 36:29.800
I was secretly squealing during their scenes together!

723
36:30.750 --> 36:32.280
The gassing up isn't personal, right?

724
36:32.560 --> 36:34.000
Not at all, Wut.

725
36:34.130 --> 36:36.850
At first, their chemistry was that of a ghost ship.

726
36:36.870 --> 36:39.230
But now, they're real.

727
36:39.250 --> 36:39.840
Ugh!

728
36:39.980 --> 36:41.740
The shippers are about to be brain-rotted!

729
36:42.560 --> 36:44.160
The brain rot, the brain rot...

730
36:44.660 --> 36:46.080
Don't get carried away with the teasing.

731
36:46.150 --> 36:47.620
If Wan decides against the role,

732
36:47.640 --> 36:49.240
I'm blaming you two.

733
36:50.080 --> 36:50.800
Good.

734
36:51.380 --> 36:52.820
Reject the role,

735
36:53.030 --> 36:54.880
and I'll launch a new couple.

736
36:55.640 --> 36:56.760
How does ThirdWut sound?

737
36:59.630 --> 37:00.440
That's not it.

738
37:11.550 --> 37:14.380
There's still no email response

739
37:14.620 --> 37:16.220
from previous auditions.

740
37:17.270 --> 37:18.120
But tomorrow,

741
37:18.640 --> 37:22.000
you're going to an audition at 'Space Station Casting Studios.'

742
37:23.220 --> 37:24.910
Also, you have an appointment with your psychiatrist.

743
37:29.650 --> 37:30.440
Nine?

744
37:32.000 --> 37:32.710
Yes, Mama?

745
37:32.820 --> 37:34.490
You were listening, right?

746
37:37.310 --> 37:38.020
Okay.

747
37:39.340 --> 37:40.140
Let's head out.

748
37:41.770 --> 37:42.390
Come on.

749
38:09.500 --> 38:10.660
Hi...

750
38:14.230 --> 38:15.120
Hi...

751
38:43.110 --> 38:44.930
Finally, we can watch this together.

752
38:47.770 --> 38:48.780
Mm.

753
38:48.960 --> 38:51.400
So many ways to interpret it now that we're watching it again, huh?

754
38:53.780 --> 38:54.890
As you mature,

755
38:54.910 --> 38:56.210
your mindset changes.

756
38:58.120 --> 39:00.000
Though my feelings for you

757
39:00.170 --> 39:01.880
never change!

758
39:06.510 --> 39:07.800
So delusional.

759
39:10.330 --> 39:12.320
Do you like it, though? Hm?

760
39:23.010 --> 39:26.200
♫Just a gentle, gentle gaze♫

761
39:26.220 --> 39:27.520
♫On me, on me♫

762
39:27.540 --> 39:29.660
♫Keep your eyes on me♫

763
39:29.680 --> 39:30.560
I'm hungry.

764
39:35.130 --> 39:36.220
What should we eat?

765
39:36.840 --> 39:38.180
Leave it to your chef.

766
39:38.370 --> 39:41.000
♫Keep your eyes on me♫

767
39:41.020 --> 39:43.380
♫On me, on me♫

768
39:45.730 --> 39:48.020
What should we eat?

769
39:52.440 --> 39:53.440
How about KFC?

770
39:54.150 --> 39:54.860
Good idea.

771
39:56.050 --> 39:56.810
When I was little,

772
39:56.830 --> 39:58.410
I wanted to be the colonel so much.

773
40:03.170 --> 40:04.720
Stop being so delusional...

774
40:06.140 --> 40:07.140
Don't you like it?

775
40:11.510 --> 40:12.560
Just go place an order.

776
40:20.100 --> 40:22.240
Here, I'm gonna take these two pieces, right?

777
40:22.650 --> 40:23.840
And this.

778
40:24.050 --> 40:25.280
- Looks yummy. - One.

779
40:32.350 --> 40:32.950
Here.

780
40:38.640 --> 40:39.720
What did you do?

781
40:39.930 --> 40:41.520
I made you a heart.

782
40:42.580 --> 40:44.050
Wholeheartedly delicious.

783
40:44.440 --> 40:45.680
Enjoy your food!

784
40:47.640 --> 40:48.760
It doesn't look like a heart.

785
40:49.620 --> 40:51.190
That’s because you can't design how love turns out.

786
40:55.950 --> 40:56.770
Wait!

787
40:58.040 --> 41:01.600
I'm gonna show you how to eat and make the client choose you.

788
41:03.190 --> 41:03.840
How?

789
41:03.860 --> 41:05.340
Like this!

790
41:08.270 --> 41:09.200
Hm!

791
41:09.610 --> 41:10.660
Try it.

792
41:11.470 --> 41:12.570
Mm!

793
41:13.780 --> 41:14.640
Adorable.

794
41:15.040 --> 41:16.080
The chicken nuggets are.

795
41:16.360 --> 41:17.520
So are you.

796
41:22.920 --> 41:24.250
If I were the client,

797
41:24.450 --> 41:26.440
I'd choose you as my brand representative for sure.

798
41:29.270 --> 41:31.120
Let me trouble you with it, then, Mr. Client.

799
41:56.050 --> 41:57.250
Mm!

800
42:05.720 --> 42:07.080
[Screenplay: Episode 1]

801
42:11.690 --> 42:13.470
Isn't Time too observant?

802
42:14.310 --> 42:15.770
I don't even know about some things.

803
42:17.990 --> 42:19.520
It's the writer's spirit.

804
42:19.930 --> 42:21.480
We just don't realize it.

805
42:22.230 --> 42:23.000
That's true.

806
42:24.000 --> 42:25.770
The storytelling is so much fun, though.

807
42:27.130 --> 42:29.780
The leads are also adorable, but...

808
42:30.170 --> 42:31.920
I don't think we're that adorable?

809
42:32.090 --> 42:33.460
We're probably even more adorable.

810
42:34.290 --> 42:35.720
You just don't realize it.

811
42:37.790 --> 42:39.520
Don't try to flirt.

812
42:39.900 --> 42:41.800
You can't charm me, Third.

813
42:50.990 --> 42:52.320
Aren't you guys too lovey-dovey?

814
42:56.930 --> 42:58.200
We'll sit properly.

815
42:58.880 --> 43:00.080
I don't mind.

816
43:00.100 --> 43:01.510
Sit wherever you want.

817
43:01.540 --> 43:03.800
As long as your relationship doesn't ruin the work.

818
43:06.820 --> 43:07.500
You mean it?

819
43:07.520 --> 43:08.400
Mm.

820
43:13.580 --> 43:16.880
You need to be considerate of other people, though.

821
43:17.210 --> 43:19.120
This is gonna rot my brain.

822
43:24.000 --> 43:26.000
Hey, get down and sit properly, Wan!

823
43:27.110 --> 43:29.040
If Wut comes in, we're all doomed.

824
43:29.360 --> 43:30.040
I'm not scared.

825
43:30.110 --> 43:31.130
I fucking am.

826
43:32.430 --> 43:33.500
If I lose my job,

827
43:33.520 --> 43:34.840
no one's gonna manage Wan.

828
43:39.020 --> 43:39.680
Read your script.

829
43:39.700 --> 43:41.160
Chop-chop. Get it over with.

830
43:42.130 --> 43:43.680
You have 11 episodes left.

831
44:08.640 --> 44:09.320
Hey,

832
44:09.650 --> 44:11.280
when are you free these days?

833
44:12.870 --> 44:14.640
I'm kinda free. Why?

834
44:17.200 --> 44:18.560
My mom wants to meet you.

835
44:18.920 --> 44:19.550
Huh?

836
44:20.320 --> 44:21.200
Seriously?

837
44:21.370 --> 44:22.000
Mm,

838
44:22.550 --> 44:24.760
she told me to bring you to see her.

839
44:25.340 --> 44:26.530
I already told my mom

840
44:27.330 --> 44:28.520
that you're my boyfriend.

841
44:31.520 --> 44:32.520
Whoa,

842
44:33.770 --> 44:35.400
I haven't even said yes.

843
44:35.770 --> 44:36.630
You're full of it.

844
44:37.140 --> 44:38.800
Are you really not gonna be my boyfriend?

845
44:40.780 --> 44:42.110
What?

846
44:43.530 --> 44:44.480
Wan...

847
44:48.850 --> 44:49.920
Will you be my boyfriend?

848
44:54.660 --> 44:55.360
Mm.

849
44:56.390 --> 44:57.720
Say yes properly.

850
44:57.830 --> 44:58.600
"Yes properly."

851
44:58.810 --> 45:00.120
Don't...

852
45:00.980 --> 45:01.680
I will.

853
45:01.930 --> 45:04.480
Shouldn’t it be a little more touching?

854
45:10.560 --> 45:12.280
Yes, Mr. Third,

855
45:14.620 --> 45:16.530
I will be your boyfriend.

856
45:23.170 --> 45:24.020
Is that good enough?

857
45:24.040 --> 45:25.520
I'm going back to the novel.

858
45:35.710 --> 45:36.890
"Then..."

859
45:38.440 --> 45:40.430
"Tle loosened his embrace,

860
45:40.870 --> 45:43.840
grabbing my shoulders so we faced each other again.

861
45:44.480 --> 45:48.230
A sly grin painted over his bowed lips."

862
45:48.250 --> 45:49.630
"Cheer me up, please."

863
45:51.010 --> 45:52.010
"A peck on the cheek?"

864
45:53.700 --> 45:54.700
"That's not enough.

865
45:55.830 --> 45:57.000
Let me kiss you."

866
45:58.580 --> 46:00.720
"He said with anticipation."

867
46:04.320 --> 46:06.100
I want to play this scene with you.

868
46:06.880 --> 46:08.520
Do you think they'll add it to the script?

869
46:09.000 --> 46:09.900
Which scene?

870
46:10.220 --> 46:11.220
This one,

871
46:11.620 --> 46:12.620
the NC scene.

872
46:15.120 --> 46:16.930
Can we rehearse it as the novel says?

873
46:26.000 --> 46:27.550
Cheer me up, please.

874
46:29.610 --> 46:30.710
You mean, a peck on the cheek?

875
46:33.340 --> 46:34.300
That's not enough.

876
46:35.040 --> 46:36.120
Let me kiss you.

877
46:38.740 --> 46:39.680
Mm.

878
46:42.800 --> 46:47.020
♫I think you've gotten me hooked so well♫

879
46:47.040 --> 46:51.220
♫My heart is under your spell♫

880
46:51.240 --> 46:55.220
♫Everything I'm feeling profoundly,♫

881
46:55.240 --> 46:59.990
♫You make it special just by being next to me♫

882
47:14.850 --> 47:16.760
- Surprise! - Surprise!

883
47:16.880 --> 47:18.040
Dad, Mom, how did you get here?

884
47:18.110 --> 47:18.990
Oh, what a strange question.

885
47:19.010 --> 47:20.650
Of course, your dad drove us here.

886
47:20.670 --> 47:21.740
- Yeah. - Let's go inside, honey.

887
47:21.760 --> 47:23.440
But...Wan isn't even up.

888
47:23.520 --> 47:24.160
Oh...

889
47:24.600 --> 47:25.600
Wan!

890
47:25.850 --> 47:27.480
Wan, Dad and Mom are here!

891
47:27.820 --> 47:29.440
Wan, are you finally awake?!

892
47:30.550 --> 47:31.730
Are you?!

893
47:32.350 --> 47:33.350
Wan!

894
47:33.370 --> 47:34.420
Dad and Mom are here!

895
47:40.320 --> 47:41.210
Don't!

896
47:45.650 --> 47:46.870
See? He's still asleep.

897
47:46.920 --> 47:47.920
Hang on.

898
47:48.110 --> 47:48.960
Why are you screaming?

899
47:48.980 --> 47:50.200
We're just out here.

900
47:50.760 --> 47:52.400
My eardrums are about to go flying.

901
47:52.420 --> 47:53.440
- Mm, come on. - Jeez... Come on.

902
47:54.630 --> 47:55.130
Shit...

903
47:55.150 --> 47:55.730
Shit...

904
47:56.890 --> 47:58.650
- Move, move. Out of the way. - Go, go, go, go.

905
47:58.770 --> 47:59.630
He's not awake...

906
47:59.650 --> 48:00.230
Wan, sweetie,

907
48:00.250 --> 48:01.210
how come you're still asleep?

908
48:01.230 --> 48:02.240
- Huh, Wan? - Ugh, Mom!

909
48:02.420 --> 48:04.180
You're not noticing one thing about your baby girl.

910
48:04.200 --> 48:05.390
Look, I got hair extensions.

911
48:05.410 --> 48:06.400
Isn't it pretty?

912
48:06.570 --> 48:08.380
Let me see. Hey, honey. Look!

913
48:09.700 --> 48:10.810
- Do you like it? - My sweet daughter,

914
48:10.830 --> 48:12.610
you're always beautiful. You take after Mom.

915
48:13.180 --> 48:14.160
You can say that again.

916
48:15.300 --> 48:15.930
Shirt!

917
48:15.960 --> 48:17.480
- Shoes first. - The slippers?

918
48:17.520 --> 48:18.330
- Whoa! - Wan...

919
48:18.740 --> 48:19.600
Dad,

920
48:19.840 --> 48:23.200
I just realized that there's a giant cockroach in my room!

921
48:23.360 --> 48:25.300
Shoo it away for me. I'm scared.

922
48:26.640 --> 48:27.370
There, there.

923
48:27.390 --> 48:28.740
- That room. - Come on, honey.

924
48:28.760 --> 48:30.470
It's just a little cockroach...

925
48:30.490 --> 48:31.620
- Just go. - It's gigantic.

926
48:31.640 --> 48:32.660
- Wan! - Whoa, Mom!

927
48:32.680 --> 48:33.360
Is he still...

928
48:33.950 --> 48:34.560
It's massive.

929
48:34.580 --> 48:36.190
We as a family have to catch it.

930
48:36.210 --> 48:37.950
What? Your dad alone can take care of it.

931
48:37.970 --> 48:39.120
- I'm serious. - Alright, where are you, cockroach?

932
48:39.140 --> 48:40.100
Show yourself.

933
48:40.120 --> 48:40.860
- Where is it? - I swear, it's here.

934
48:40.880 --> 48:42.070
- Where is it? - Where?

935
48:42.090 --> 48:43.650
Go, go, go, go, go.

936
48:43.670 --> 48:45.610
- Has it gone under the table? - I saw it over there.

937
48:45.630 --> 48:47.020
I'm not seeing it, sweetie.

938
48:49.310 --> 48:49.940
Is it actually here?

939
48:49.960 --> 48:52.840
We have bug sprays for a reason, you know?

940
48:52.900 --> 48:53.850
Do you have one in your room?

941
48:53.870 --> 48:54.440
Where is it, sweetie?

942
49:00.520 --> 49:01.600
Oh, Third.

943
49:06.870 --> 49:07.960
You just arrived?

944
49:10.580 --> 49:11.360
I did.

945
49:12.320 --> 49:12.970
Huh?

946
49:13.490 --> 49:14.460
- Right. - You did...

947
49:14.480 --> 49:15.740
Right, you just did. Then...

948
49:15.760 --> 49:17.100
Want some noodle soup? I brought it for you guys.

949
49:17.120 --> 49:18.070
Wow, that'd be great, Mom.

950
49:18.090 --> 49:19.450
I was just getting hungry.

951
49:20.050 --> 49:22.360
Did you actually... come here in that outfit, sweetie?

952
49:22.380 --> 49:23.520
A T-shirt and shorts?

953
49:24.260 --> 49:25.040
Oh, well...

954
49:25.240 --> 49:26.300
It's a typical day, Mom,

955
49:26.320 --> 49:27.860
so this is what I went with.

956
49:28.380 --> 49:30.630
And why is your hair so messy?

957
49:30.650 --> 49:31.790
Uh...

958
49:31.810 --> 49:32.720
I was in a rush!

959
49:34.240 --> 49:36.480
It's just that I didn't blow-dry my hair...sir.

960
49:36.640 --> 49:39.580
Right, so you washed your hair and took a motorcycle taxi here?

961
49:39.600 --> 49:40.360
- Uh... - Is that so?

962
49:40.380 --> 49:42.160
- Yes. - And while you were on it, you were...

963
49:42.180 --> 49:43.920
swerving left, right, left, right,

964
49:43.940 --> 49:45.080
and that's how you got a pompadour on both sides?

965
49:45.280 --> 49:46.600
- Ugh! - Right...

966
49:46.620 --> 49:48.360
That's enough. Just go sit and chill.

967
49:48.380 --> 49:51.180
What? So do you have a bug spray?

968
49:51.200 --> 49:52.970
- So I can... - Dad, Mom, hello.

969
49:53.230 --> 49:53.740
Oh...

970
49:55.510 --> 49:57.640
Oh, Third. What's up, man?

971
49:58.130 --> 49:59.450
Yo, man!

972
50:00.090 --> 50:01.320
- Come on, come on. - Right.

973
50:01.840 --> 50:03.050
Sit, sit, sit.

974
50:04.240 --> 50:05.800
Alright, we're sitting. Alright, alright.

975
50:11.350 --> 50:12.740
Eat up, kids.

976
50:16.090 --> 50:17.520
Blow it first. Careful, it's hot.

977
50:18.570 --> 50:20.440
There, you keep picking them out, Wan.

978
50:21.270 --> 50:22.720
Why aren't you eating the veggies, sweetie?

979
50:23.060 --> 50:23.660
Uh...

980
50:24.130 --> 50:25.360
I like veggies.

981
